    "body": "> If child is null, this prepends node as the first child.\r\n\r\nwith `insertBefore`, if `child` is `null` the element is appended (like `appendChild` would do) ... I find this proposed behavior here a bit controversial ... the *before* \"*appends* with null, the *after* \"*prepend*\" with null as first child ... am I the only one not fully getting the use case for prepending as first child with a method called *after* ?",
